# Thinkway Enterprise Platform Architecture v1.0 (Frozen)

**Milestone:** `docs/architecture/THINKWAY_ENTERPRISE_PLATFORM_ARCHITECTURE_V1.md`  
**Compliance template:** `docs/architecture/PLATFORM_ARCHITECTURE_COMPLIANCE.md`  
**Package:** `docs/architecture/platform-ux/` (docs 01–12 frozen)

## Product definition

Thinkway is a **campaign-centric enterprise operating system**. The campaign is the single business object; the campaign lifecycle is the single business process. Stakeholder journeys enter that lifecycle at different stages. Nothing may exist outside this model.

## Frozen — do not redefine

- Navigation philosophy (Platform → Module → Business Process → Content)
- Workspace philosophy / Campaign Lifecycle Architecture (doc 12)
- Stakeholder Journey Architecture (doc 11)
- Enterprise UX standards / Financial Display Standard
- Campaign Module Baseline pillars (Enterprise Tabs evolve, not replaced)

**No architectural redesign** unless Product formally reopens Architecture v1.0.

## Mandatory for every ADR / release architecture / implementation proposal

Include section **Platform Architecture Compliance** covering:

1. Lifecycle stages affected (S00–S18 from doc 12)  
2. Stakeholder journeys affected  
3. Workspace(s) extended  
4. Baseline documents referenced  
5. Why no new navigation philosophy  
6. Why no duplicate workflow  
7. How the feature extends the campaign lifecycle  

## Implementation posture

- Extend the baseline; do not reinvent it.  
- Authorized migration phases only (currently Phase 1 when in progress).  
- Presentation/IA changes must inherit frozen architecture.  
- No new architecture docs unless a genuine enterprise-wide capability requires one (and compliance section is present).  
- Functional priority after Phase 1: Planning Board → Copilot → Client/Vendor/Creator journeys → Reporting → Notifications → Analytics.
